                <pb facs="0112" n="104" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg104"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751.62/500: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-11-26T13:00:00+00:00">November 26, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 26—10:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2001. Personal for the Under Secretary. Reference to my telegram No. 1994,
                    November 25, 7 p.m. Bonnet asked me to send you a personal word of his hope that
                    you would understand and sympathize with the reasons which moved him to conclude
                    the declaration with Germany.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
